    },
    "message": "Do not recompute the hashes capture() has just computed\n\nCheckpoint.capture() computes state_hash and checkpoint_hash from the\nworld and body documents it just built, then _validate() serialized the\nwhole history twice more to compare the same objects with those hashes.\ncapture() now skips only those two comparisons. Schema, structure and\nthe WorldState/metrics restore checks still run, and every later read or\nsave_branch still verifies both hashes, so mutation after capture is\ndetected as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
